01:01 The burden of the word of HaSHEM to Yisra'el by Mal'akhi.
01:02 I have loved you, says HaSHEM. Yet you say, Wherein have you loved us? Was not Esav Ya`akov's brother, says HaSHEM: yet I loved Ya`akov;
01:03 but Esav I hated, and made his mountains a desolation, and gave his heritage to the jackals of the wilderness.
01:04 Whereas Edom says, We are beaten down, but we will return and build the waste places; thus says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, They shall build, but I will throw down; and men shall call them The border of wickedness, and The people against whom HaSHEM has indignation forever.
01:05 Your eyes shall see, and you shall say, HaSHEM be magnified beyond the border of Yisra'el.
01:06 A son honors his father, and a servant his master: if then I am a father, where is my honor? and if I am a master, where is my fear? says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot to you, Cohanim, who despise my name. You say, Wherein have we despised your name?
01:07 You offer polluted bread on my altar. You say, Wherein have we polluted you? In that you say, The table of HaSHEM is contemptible.
01:08 When you offer the blind for sacrifice, it is no evil! and when you offer the lame and sick, it is no evil! Present it now to your governor; will he be pleased with you? or will he accept your person? says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
01:09 Now, please entreat the favor of G-D, that he may be gracious to us: this has been by your means: will he accept any of your persons? says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
01:10 Oh that there were one among you who would shut the doors, that you might not kindle fire on my altar in vain! I have no pleasure in you, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, neither will I accept an offering at your hand.
01:11 For from the rising of the sun even to the going down of the same my name shall be great among the Goyim; and in every place incense shall be offered to my name, and a pure offering: for my name shall be great among the Goyim, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
01:12 But you profane it, in that you say, The table of HaSHEM is polluted, and the fruit of it, even its food, is contemptible.
01:13 You say also, Behold, what a weariness is it! and you have snuffed at it, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot; and you have brought that which was taken by violence, and the lame, and the sick; thus you bring the offering: should I accept this at your hand? says HaSHEM.
01:14 But cursed be the deceiver, who has in his flock a male, and vows, and sacrifices to the L-rd a blemished thing; for I am a great King, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, and my name is awesome among the Goyim.  
02:01 Now, you Cohanim, this commandment is for you.
02:02 If you will not hear, and if you will not lay it to heart, to give glory to my name, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, then will I send the curse on you, and I will curse your blessings; yes, I have cursed them already, because you do not lay it to heart.
02:03 Behold, I will rebuke your seed, and will spread dung on your faces, even the dung of your feasts; and you shall be taken away with it.
02:04 You shall know that I have sent this commandment to you, that my covenant may be with Levi, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
02:05 My covenant was with him of life and shalom; and I gave them to him who he might fear; and he feared me, and stood in awe of my name.
02:06 The law of truth was in his mouth, and unrighteousness was not found in his lips: he walked with me in shalom and uprightness, and turned many away from iniquity.
02:07 For the Cohen's lips should keep knowledge, and they should seek the law at his mouth; for he is the messenger of HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
02:08 But you are turned aside out of the way; you have caused many to stumble in the law; you have corrupted the covenant of Levi, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
02:09 Therefore have I also made you contemptible and base before all the people, according as you have not kept my ways, but have had respect of persons in the law.
02:10 Don't we all have one father? has not one G-D created us? why do we deal treacherously every man against his brother, profaning the covenant of our fathers?
02:11 Yehudah has dealt treacherously, and an abomination is committed in Yisra'el and in Yerushalayim; for Yehudah has profaned the holiness of HaSHEM which he loves, and has married the daughter of a foreign god.
02:12 HaSHEM will cut off, to the man who does this, him who wakes and him who answers, out of the tents of Ya`akov, and him who offers an offering to HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
02:13 This again you do: you cover the altar of HaSHEM with tears, with weeping, and with sighing, because he doesn't regard the offering any more, neither receives it with good will at your hand.
02:14 Yet you say, Why? Because HaSHEM has been witness between you and the wife of your youth, against whom you have dealt treacherously, though she is your companion, and the wife of your covenant.
02:15 Did he not make one, although he had the residue of the Spirit? Why one? He sought a godly seed. Therefore take heed to your spirit, and let none deal treacherously against the wife of his youth.
02:16 For I hate putting away, says HaSHEM, the G-D of Yisra'el, and him who covers his garment with violence, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot: therefore take heed to your spirit, that you don't deal treacherously.
02:17 You have wearied HaSHEM with your words. Yet you say, Wherein have we wearied him? In that you say, Everyone who does evil is good in the sight of HaSHEM, and he delights in them; or where is the G-D of justice? 
03:01 Behold, I send my messenger, and he shall prepare the way before me: and the L-rd, whom you seek, will suddenly come to his temple; and the messenger of the covenant, whom you desire, behold, he comes, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
03:02 But who can abide the day of his coming? and who shall stand when he appears? for he is like a refiner's fire, and like fuller's soap:
03:03 and he will sit as a refiner and purifier of silver, and he will purify the sons of Levi, and refine them as gold and silver; and they shall offer to HaSHEM offerings in righteousness.
03:04 Then shall the offering of Yehudah and Yerushalayim be pleasant to HaSHEM, as in the days of old, and as in ancient years.
03:05 I will come near to you to judgment; and I will be a swift witness against the sorcerers, and against the adulterers, and against the perjurers, and against those who oppress the hireling in his wages, the widow, and the fatherless, and who turn aside the sojourner from his right, and don't fear me, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
03:06 For I, HaSHEM, don't change; therefore you, sons of Ya`akov, are not consumed.
03:07 From the days of your fathers you have turned aside from my ordinances, and have not kept them. Return to me, and I will return to you, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot. But you say, Wherein shall we return?
03:08 Will a man rob G-D? yet you rob me. But you say, Wherein have we robbed you? In tithes and offerings.
03:09 You are cursed with the curse; for you rob me, even this whole nation.
03:10 Bring the whole tithe into the store-house, that there may be food in my house, and prove me now herewith, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, if I will not open you the windows of Heaven, and pour you out a blessing, that there shall not be room enough to receive it.
03:11 I will rebuke the devourer for your sakes, and he shall not destroy the fruits of your ground; neither shall your vine cast its fruit before the time in the field, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
03:12 All nations shall call you happy; for you shall be a delightful land, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
03:13 Your words have been stout against me, says HaSHEM. Yet you say, What have we spoken against you?
03:14 You have said, It is vain to serve G-D; and what profit is it that we have kept his charge, and that we have walked mournfully before HaSHEM-Tzva'ot?
03:15 Now we call the proud happy; yes, those who work wickedness are built up; yes, they tempt G-D, and escape.
03:16 Then those who feared HaSHEM spoke one with another; and HaSHEM listened, and heard, and a book of memory was written before him, for those who feared HaSHEM, and that thought on his name.
03:17 They shall be my, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, even my own possession, in the day that I make; and I will spare them, as a man spares his own son who serves him.
03:18 Then shall you return and discern between the righteous and the wicked, between him who serves G-D and him who doesn't serve him.  *
03:19 For, behold, the day comes, it burns as a furnace; and all the proud, and all who work wickedness, shall be stubble; and the day that comes shall burn them up, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot, that it shall leave them neither root nor branch.
03:20 But to you who fear my name shall the sun of righteousness arise with healing in its wings; and you shall go forth, and gambol as calves of the stall.
03:21 You shall tread down the wicked; for they shall be ashes under the soles of your feet in the day that I make, says HaSHEM-Tzva'ot.
03:22 Remember you the law of Moshe my servant, which I commanded to him in Chorev for all Yisra'el, even statutes and ordinances.
03:23 Behold, I will send you Eliyah the prophet before the great and terrible day of HaSHEM come.
03:24 He shall turn the heart of the fathers to the children, and the heart of the children to their fathers; lest I come and strike the earth with a curse.  
